; A daemon has a lifetime, and a cram file cannot own one: a session snapshot's
; expected output is fixed, while this case must skip where no sshd is installed
; and fail where one was expected. Neither is expressible as a snapshot, so the
; test is a script whose exit code is the verdict and whose output is what gets
; read when it fails.

; CI is named rather than inherited. Passing it through explicitly is what makes
; it a dependency of this rule: a run that skipped because no sshd was installed
; is then not the cached answer to the run that must fail because CI is set.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (:script ssh_real_sshd.sh))
 (action
  (setenv
   CI
   %{env:CI=}
   (run bash %{script} %{bin:bondi-client}))))
